    "metadata_separator": "\n",
    "text": "However, this era is facing a chip shortage due to strong demand and no supply. This goes back to\nCOVID-19 lockdowns in the second quarter of 2020, when demand for work-from-home technology\nincreased exponentially and automakers found themselves competing for the semiconductor\ncapacities located in Asian foundries (J. P. Morgan, 2022). Furthermore, on the 9th August, 2022 US\nPresident Biden signed the CHIPS and Science Act of 2022 (the \u201cCHIPS Plus Act\u201d) (H. R. 4346 The\nCHIPS and Science Act of 2022). \nThe CHIPS Plus Act provides substantial opportunities and financial incentives to manufacturers in\nthe semiconductor supply chain. It amends legislation and appropriates funding for semiconductor\nincentives originally in the National Defence Authorization Act (\u201cNDAA\u201d) for 2021 (117th Congress\nPublic Law, 2022).",
    "mimetype": "text/plain",
